---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy — Zipizy"
  description="How Zipizy processes files, stores preferences and makes network requests."
>
  <Header />
  <main>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>Updated 9 October 2026</p>
    <h2>Your files and text</h2>
    <p>
      PDF, image, text, QR and developer tools process inputs on your device.
      Zipizy does not upload those inputs to a processing server. There is no
      account system.
    </p>
    <h2>Tools that use the internet</h2>
    <p>
      YouTube and Vimeo thumbnail tools contact those services to retrieve video
      information or images. Those providers receive the requested video
      identifier or URL and connection information such as your IP address.
      These tools do not work offline.
    </p>
    <h2>Desktop app</h2>
    <p>
      The desktop app serves bundled tools locally and includes no analytics or
      advertising. Opening a GitHub, support or other external link opens your
      browser. Downloads are saved where you choose. Your operating system may
      retain downloaded files.
    </p>
    <h2>Preferences and the website</h2>
    <p>
      Your light/dark preference is stored locally as zipizy-theme. This release
      does not include analytics or advertising scripts. A host serving the web
      version may keep normal connection logs; its policy applies to those
      requests.
    </p>
    <h2>Sharing a bug report</h2>
    <p>
      Issues on the public repository can be read by anyone. Use sample data and
      remove passwords or personal information from attachments. If you email
      us, we receive the information you include.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="mailto:denethraveesha@gmail.com">denethraveesha@gmail.com</a>
    </p>
  </main>
  <style>
    main {
      max-width: 760px;
      margin: auto;
      padding: 40px 24px;
    }
    h2 {
      font-size: 22px;
      margin-top: 32px;
    }
    p {
      line-height: 1.8;
      color: var(--text-secondary);
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
